# SPA DRAG — 5857-line JS, dead homepage, dogfight
File: website/audit/spa-drag.oot

Verdict: FAIL-CLOSED on Boyd drag. The SPA overwrites the
static homepage. Most of src/main.js is a canvas dogfight.
WORKFLOW.oot §0.3 asks for a monochrome monospace UI.

## 1. Two homepages

index.html <main id="content"> holds six <details> cards
(ooda, std, opm, cli, lsp, mcp) plus SVG diagrams.
On load, renderRoute() fetches /pulled/openOODA.json and
sets contentEl.innerHTML. The static cards are discarded.

No-JS and crawlers see the static cards (live fetch of
https://openooda.org/ returned those cards).
JS users see pulled/openOODA.json markdown.

The two views disagree: static still says "cli"; JSON says
eight repos and omits website/packaging/.github.

Subtractive fix: pick one homepage. Either delete the static
cards and ship real markup, or stop the SPA from replacing
#content on the default route.

## 2. What src/main.js actually is

Approximate mass (line ranges):

| Lines | Concern |
|-------|---------|
| 1–92 | routes, markdown, install HTML |
| 93–527 | pools, theme LUT, copy button |
| 528–5550 | dogfight: gens 1–7, weapons, rAF |
| 5553–5621 | renderRoute |
| 5623–5857 | hash router, theme, mail, sky |

The product (router + markdown + theme + install) is under
400 lines. The dogfight is about 5000 lines.
src/ANCHOR.oo says splitting would "add import plumbing".
The 256-line law does not grant that exception.

WORKFLOW.oot §0.3: monochrome UI, monospace type.
Nine theme palettes and a fighter-jet sim are extra weight.
Gen 7 "singularity cannon" is marketing on a public page.

## 3. WASM residue

renderRoute is wrapped to ignore ooda_app_route() from a WASM
instance. Comments say the WASM route table is stale.
window.wasmActive still drives theme_next if present.
No WASM module is loaded from this repo.
That is dead interface (RULES 1.1 anti-shortcut / Red 3).

## 4. Copy button vs markup

INSTALL_HTML uses class "copy".
index.html static box uses id="copy".
setupOpenOODA() binds main .copy. After SPA replace, the
JSON homepage uses INSTALL_HTML, so the class matches.
Before replace, the static button id="copy" is unbound.
Another reason to delete one of the two homepages.

## 5. Missing packaging route

README.md lists 11 repos. Nav lists 8:
openOODA, ooda, std, opm, lsp, mcp, oodar, oodac.
packaging/ and website/ have no pulled page.
.github/ is an org profile, not a product surface.

## 6. Recommended subtractive sequence

Do this in website/ only. Do not wait on oodac.

1. Delete the dogfight and the sky canvas. Keep gen-bar only
   if it still has a product meaning. It does not.
2. Stop replacing #content on the default route, or delete
   the static cards. One homepage.
3. Split remaining JS along seams until each file is
   <= 256 lines: route, markdown, theme, install.
   New files must be .oo if a generator exists. Until then,
   do not add a second .js. Prefer pre-rendered HTML from
   .oot so the .js file can shrink to a theme toggle.
4. Add packaging to the nav only after a pulled .oot page
   exists with a true tag.

E-M effect: remove ~5000 lines of D (drag), keep the install
line and the eight repo pages. That is the 80/20 cut.
